{title: Bread of Life}
{subtitle: John 6:22–59; 8:12}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Bb] | [Cm] | [Ab] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
They [Eb]followed him across the sea
They'd [Abmaj7]eaten loaves and fish for free
They [Cm]asked him for another sign [Bb]
Like [Ab]manna in the olden time
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]I am the bread of life
Whoever [Cm]comes to me will never hunger
[Ab]And whoever believes in [Bb]me will never [Ab]thirst
I am the bread of [Eb][Bb]life [Cm][Ab]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Not the [Eb]bread that fades by noon
Not the [Abmaj7]feast that ends too soon
[Cm]Broken here for all to share [Bb]
[Ab]Bread of heaven, everywhere
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]I am the bread of life
Whoever [Cm]comes to me will never hunger
[Ab]And whoever believes in [Bb]me will never [Ab]thirst
I am the bread of [Eb][Bb]life
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Bb] | [Cm7] | [Cm7] | [Ab] |
| [Ab] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]I am the light of the [Eb]world
Whoever [Cm7]follows me will never [Ab]walk in darkness
But will have the [Bb]light of [Ab]life
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]I am the bread of life
[Cm7]I am the bread of life
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Cm7] | [Ab] | [Bb] | [Ab] |
| [Ab] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Cm7] |
| [Ab] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
